I was born in Leesburg Virginia and I've  actually lived there for 14 years until  I moved to a place called Alexandria  Virginia which is right outside DC so  sort of just been hanging out in one  state for my entire life and I now go to  the University of Virginia and I've  taken a little bit of time off to do  YouTube  right when clash of clans came out I  knew it was going to be such a  successful game even though it was  really in the infant stages and only had  maybe 5,000 likes on Facebook I know  after I played for two days and I texted  my friends who are at their schools I  said you guys have to download this game  this game's gonna be big so we all got  together we're all in our clan  there's games look like cut the rope and  stuff like that that you play for fun  while maybe you're waiting for five  minutes but I never really seen a game  like clash on mobile Age of Empires was  one of my favorite games growing up and  you sort of build your town and your  village and right when I downloaded  clash I got that feel that I'm  progressing I'm building my village and  that's what made it so addictive I've  been playing it I think for two weeks in  the game and been out for maybe a month  and I was looking for single-player  level maps online to see if someone had  done a walkthrough and I had no  experience with YouTube whatsoever  besides looking at cat videos and stuff  like that so I saw that no one had done  the levels and it was something I was  interested I was like oh I could do some  single-player guides and then slowly the  community said hey we want to see some  multiplayer battles and even though I  was new at the game it was fun to make  content fun to interact with the  community and just keep like making  friends I made my giant clan system from  there and then the game just exploded  and then from there a lot of other  youtubers came around and now it's been  fun being able to travel do clash of  clans stuff and a bunch of different  cities going up to Finland to visit the  supercell headquarters which is amazing  every single time and I've had an  awesome time  I think I had maybe one subscriber after  the second day and I remember telling my  friends and I told my friends I knew  they were messing with me because one of  them was a subscriber like I didn't  believe that people were actually  subscribing to my YouTube channel let  alone watching my videos I saw clash  grow as a game and then mic my channel  obviously grew with that as well as the  other people that started making YouTube  videos with me so right now I think I'm  at 1.1 million subscribers on my channel  and I know there's a lot of other  channels that are growing above a  hundred thousands so it's really  starting to like make an amazing  community on YouTube and it's something  that really mobile gaming hasn't seen  before
 

